WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.465
Listing your first product is an exciting step in your seller journey.

00:00:04.465 --> 00:00:10.419
To set yourself up for success, we recommend reviewing our pre-listing checklist before you get

00:00:10.419 --> 00:00:10.791
started.

00:00:10.791 --> 00:00:16.000
There are a few ways to list your first product, depending on your needs.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.760
We encourage you to review and understand all your options, as you will likely want to list products

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.000
in different ways throughout your selling journey.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.500
First, let's review the two basic types of product listings, existing and new.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:36.000
Existing products are items that are already in the Amazon catalog.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:43.238
When customers shop in the Amazon store, they are able to see all seller offers on a single product

00:00:43.238 --> 00:00:44.000
detail page.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.476
This helps customers find the products they want and compare offers and saves you from having to

00:00:50.476 --> 00:00:52.000
recreate product detail pages.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:58.000
When you list an existing product, you'll be adding your offer to an existing product detail page.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.048
We refer to this as matching a listing.

00:01:01.048 --> 00:01:06.000
New product listings are items that are not in the Amazon catalog yet.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.684
When listing a new product, you'll need to fill out all the product information in addition to your

00:01:11.684 --> 00:01:12.000
offer.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.811
We refer to this as creating a listing.

00:01:14.811 --> 00:01:20.784
When listing new products, your options will vary based on whether or not your product is branded.

00:01:20.784 --> 00:01:25.000
And if that brand is enrolled in Amazon Brand Registry, in general.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:31.107
If a product is part of a brand enrolled in Brand Registry, only three types of sellers can create

00:01:31.107 --> 00:01:34.000
its product detail page using the standard listing process.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.545
The original rights owner who enrolled the brand, other sellers verified as internal to the brand

00:01:40.545 --> 00:01:43.000
and resellers authorized by the brand.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:49.452
If a product is part of a brand not enrolled in Brand Registry, the product owner can create a listing

00:01:49.452 --> 00:01:53.000
for it after they secure approval for their unregistered brand name.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:59.139
Finally, if a product is generic, meaning it doesn't have a permanent brand name or logo affixed,

00:01:59.139 --> 00:02:05.639
its listing can be created by the product owner using generic as a brand name during the listing

00:02:05.639 --> 00:02:06.000
process.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:11.760
In some cases, you may be required to complete a selling application for a product or category before

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.000
you can match or create a listing.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.457
If necessary, you'll be prompted to complete that application during the listing process.

00:02:18.457 --> 00:02:23.600
Whether you're matching or creating product listings, there are two ways to list your products,

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.000
one at a time or in bulk.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.130
All sellers can list items one at a time.

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:34.000
That means you'll use a single product ID to match or create a listing.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.875
All sellers can also match or create product variations one at a time.

00:02:38.875 --> 00:02:46.000
If you have a professional selling plan, you can also match or create listings in bulk using a spreadsheet.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:57.032
Step-by-step instructions for listing new or existing products one by one or in bulk can be found

00:02:57.032 --> 00:03:03.573
in our comprehensive guide how to list your products on Seller University.
